// Dogwood port of policies/complete.cedar. complete is permitted unconditionally at
// the Policy layer: whether all of this case's items are actually recorded is a
// per-case fact neither Cedar nor Dogwood can see from here (same limitation as
// record_item -- Dogwood's documented information providers beyond its own event
// history are limited to Amazon Bedrock Guardrails, nothing for a DynamoDB-style case
// lookup; see https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock-agentcore/latest/devguide/
// policy-temporal.html, "Temporal policies"). outbound_ivr.tools.business.complete in the
// Lambda enforces the real rule -- a case with items still missing is escalated
// instead of completed, regardless of what the model claims in `summary`.
//
// Deliberately NOT a temporal "every required item was recorded this session" rule:
// Dogwood's `count`/`formerly within` operators (example-policies-temporal.html) can
// confirm that *a* record_item call happened, or that calls for a fixed, static set of
// keys happened, but not that *this case's actual* missing_items set (which varies per
// case) was fully covered -- the same case-lookup gap as record_item.cedar. Gating
// complete on the static three-key superset below would incorrectly deny completion
// for any case whose missing_items is a strict subset of that superset (the common
// case), so it is not done here; see policies/README.md.
permit(
  principal,
  action == AgentCore::Action::"OutboundIvrTools___complete",
  resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"${GATEWAY_ARN}"
) when {
  context.input has case_id &&
  context.input.case_id != ""
};
